# /usr/bin/tempio is a pre-compiled Go binary bundled inside
# ghcr.io/home-assistant/base-python by the Home Assistant team.
# These CVEs are in that upstream binary's stdlib/x/crypto and cannot
# be fixed by this project — they require a base-image update from HA.
# Track: https://github.com/home-assistant/docker-base
CVE-2024-45337
CVE-2025-68121

# GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 — "React Router: RSC Mode CSRF Bypass Allows Action
# Execution Before 400 Response" (high, no CVE assigned). Affects react-router
# >=7.12.0 <8.3.0, and there is no 7.x release without a high advisory: every
# version below 7.18.0 carries the open-redirect/XSS set fixed in 7.18.0, and
# every version from 7.12.0 up carries this one. The only patched release is
# 8.3.0, which requires React >=19.2.7 and Node >=22.22 and drops the
# react-router-dom package entirely.
#
# Not reachable here: the bug is in the unstable React Server Components APIs.
# Plenum's UI is a client-only SPA — it mounts <BrowserRouter> and uses
# <Routes>/<Route>/<NavLink> only, with no data router, loaders, actions, SSR
# or RSC anywhere in frontend/src. Nothing in the bundle can reach the
# vulnerable code path.
#
# Scoped to this one advisory ID on purpose: any *other* react-router
# advisory still fails the scan. Remove this entry when the React 19 +
# react-router 8 upgrade lands.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2
